<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37012" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pons</span></b> , ntis, m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>a geographical proper name.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Pons Argenteus, the modern
				<i>Argens</i>, Lepid. ap. <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam.
				10, 34, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">10, 35</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Pons Campanus, <i><span class="en">Hor. S. 1,
				5, 45</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 14, 6, 8, §
			62</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			Aureoli, the modern <i>Pontiruolo</i>, Trebell. XXX.
			Tyr. Aureol. al.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
